    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d207">

                <pb facs="0238" n="226" sameAs="frus:frus1945v04/pg226"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">874.00/5–2545: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the Ambassador in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Harriman</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-05-25T20:00:00-04:00">May 25, 1945—8
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1145. Please inform FonOff that at 4 a.m. May 24 Agrarian leader G. M. Dimitrov
                    sought asylum at the residence in Sofia of the United States Representative in
                    Bulgaria, who forthwith placed the matter before the Bulgarian authorities. The
                    Department has approved Barnes’ action and instructed him to seek assurances
                    that appropriate measures be taken to ensure Dimitrov’s safety.</p>
                <p>This instruction is being sent to Moscow and London;<anchor n="59"
                        xml:id="d207-f1"/> repeated to Sofia.<anchor n="60" xml:id="d207-f2"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Grew</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
